WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:07.291
You'll explain why each provider's
notices end at a person or a page,

3
00:00:07.291 --> 00:00:11.300
and why email stays an early
warning, not the system of record.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.938
You'll name the six kinds of
notice, and who owns each one.

5
00:00:14.938 --> 00:00:16.636
You'll read the record's fields,

6
00:00:16.636 --> 00:00:20.438
and tell a provider's own action date
from one the kit's rule inferred.

7
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:24.713
And you'll show that a second read of
the same notices changes no fingerprint.

8
00:00:24.713 --> 00:00:28.012
There's nothing to take first:
this is the first module.

9
00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:29.907
If you have time, read the intake,

10
00:00:29.907 --> 00:00:34.936
triage and routing chapter of Compliance
Automation and Day-Two Operations, which

11
00:00:34.936 --> 00:00:39.674
routes Microsoft's service health email
today and never acts on an email alone.

12
00:00:39.674 --> 00:00:45.863
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1 or later with
Pester 5, and a copy of the repository.

13
00:00:45.863 --> 00:00:46.850
No tenant.
